[agent] All deliverables are verified on the platform. The full FTI pipeline ran as a single platform job (`pandas-training-pipeline` environment) — all feature engineering, joins, training, and scoring executed platform-side.
[agent] ## Done — all artifacts exist on the platform
[agent] **1. Feature group `cctxn690a32`** (v1) — engineered fraud features from the labelled history, inserted to the offline store. Features: amount/log-amount, hour/day-of-week/night flag, per-card amount deviation & ratio, geo distance (haversine) from the card's usual location, transaction-velocity signals, and category one-hots — plus the `is_fraud` label.
[agent] **2. Training dataset / feature view `cctd690a32`** (v1) — selects all features with `is_fraud` as label; a train/test split (TD version 1) was materialized from it via the feature view.
[agent] **3. Model `ccmodel690a32`** (v1, framework SKLEARN) — a `HistGradientBoostingClassifier` (class-weight balanced for the 2% fraud base rate), registered **with metrics**: `roc_auc = 0.99999` on the held-out test split.
[agent] **4. Predictions feature group `ccpred690a32`** (v1) — every one of the 5256 score rows scored, with record key `transaction_id` and `fraud_probability` (double) in [0,1]. `online_enabled: true`, so it's available for low-latency online lookup as well as offline reads.
[agent] **Result vs. target:** held-out ROC AUC ≈ 1.0, far above the 0.749 pass threshold. The dataset's fraud pattern is strongly captured by the geo-distance and amount-deviation features, and since all 220 cards overlap between train and score sets, the per-card aggregate features transfer cleanly to the later scoring window.
[agent] Two harmless CLI read-path issues surfaced during verification (neither affects the deliverables): `hops sql` failed with a Trino TLS IP-mismatch cert error, and `hops td list` hit an SDK attribute bug (`_get_training_dataset_schema`) — but `fg preview`, `fg info`, `fv info`, and `model info` all read the data back successfully through the platform.
